  "description": "POV: you pick up a penny off the sidewalk. Follow it back to the Mint and see who pays the difference.\n\nSources:\n- U.S. Department of the Treasury: Penny Production Cessation FAQs: https://home.treasury.gov/news/featured-stories/penny-production-cessation-faqs\n- CoinNews: Penny costs 3.69 cents to make in 2024 (reporting the U.S. Mint 2024 annual report): https://www.coinnews.net/2025/02/10/penny-costs-3-69-cents-to-make-in-2024/\n\nFrom the cited pages: the cost to make a penny rose from 1.3 cents to 3.69 cents per penny over the past 10 years; roughly 114 billion pennies exist; the U.S. Mint projects an immediate annual saving of $56 million in reduced material costs and has stopped manufacturing new pennies; in fiscal 2024 the Mint shipped 3.172 billion cents to the Federal Reserve and reported a penny loss of $85.3 million. Our math: 3.69 - 1 = 2.69 cents lost per penny; 2.69 cents x 3.172 billion = about $85.3 million; 114 billion x 1 cent = $1.14 billion. Cash prices are not changing because of this. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #penny #money #howtheymakemoney",
